  "Karl Lagerfeld's cat Choupette was waited on by maids and earned millions of euros modelling in 2014.",
  "Karl Lagerfeld adopted Choupette in 2011 after looking after her for the model Baptiste Giabiconi.",
  "Freddie Mercury's song Delilah on the 1991 album Innuendo is about his cat of that name.",
  "Freddie Mercury dedicated his 1985 solo album Mr. Bad Guy to his cats, including Jerry, Tom, Oscar and Tiffany.",
  "Charles Dickens had the paw of his cat Bob made into a letter opener after the cat died in 1862.",
  "Charles Dickens's deaf cat was known to snuff out his candle with a paw when it wanted attention.",
  "Edgar Allan Poe's tortoiseshell cat Catterina reportedly sat on his shoulder while he wrote.",
  "William S. Burroughs wrote The Cat Inside, a 1986 book about his cats, including Ruski and Fletch.",
  "Jorge Luis Borges wrote a poem to his white cat Beppo, who was named after a poem by Lord Byron.",
  "Andy Warhol's 1950s book 25 Cats Name Sam and One Blue Pussy featured his Siamese cats, most named Sam.",
  "The painter Paul Klee was photographed many times with his white cat Bimbo in the 1930s.",
  "Henri Matisse kept cats named Minouche and Coussi, who appear in photographs of the artist at home.",
  "Louis Wain, the Victorian cat illustrator, began drawing cats to amuse his sick wife and her cat Peter.",
  "Thomas Hardy's cat Cobby is said to have disappeared the day the writer died in 1928.",
  "Albert Schweitzer is said to have written with his right hand whenever his cat Sizi fell asleep on his left arm.",
  "Cardinal Richelieu, the French statesman of the 1600s, kept more than a dozen cats and left money for their care.",
  "Florence Nightingale kept many cats over her lifetime, including a large Persian she named Bismarck.",
  "John Lennon kept cats throughout his life, including one he named Elvis after Elvis Presley.",
  "Taylor Swift's cats are named after television characters: Meredith Grey, Olivia Benson and Benjamin Button.",
  "Orangey, a ginger tabby, played the cat in Breakfast at Tiffany's and won two PATSY awards for animal actors.",
  "The original Morris, mascot of 9Lives cat food, was adopted from an animal shelter near Chicago in 1968.",
  "Grumpy Cat's real name was Tardar Sauce. Her scowl came from feline dwarfism and an underbite.",
  "Grumpy Cat became famous after her photo was posted on Reddit in September 2012.",
  "Grumpy Cat died in 2019 at the age of seven. A wax figure of her stands in Madame Tussauds in San Francisco.",
  "Lil Bub, a cat from Indiana, had dwarfism and extra toes, and her teeth never grew in, so her tongue hung out.",
  "Lil Bub raised hundreds of thousands of dollars for special-needs pets before her death in 2019.",
  "Lil Bub's genome was sequenced in a crowdfunded project that traced her condition to two rare mutations.",
  "Maru, a Scottish Fold from Japan, holds a Guinness World Record as the most watched animal on YouTube.",
  "Maru is famous for diving into cardboard boxes of every size, and his videos date back to 2008.",
  "Maru's owner has never revealed her name and posts the videos under the name mugumogu.",
  "The Keyboard Cat video was filmed in 1984 by Charlie Schmidt. The cat's name was Fatso and he died in 1987.",
  "The Keyboard Cat clip became a meme in 2009, used to play off people who had embarrassed themselves on video.",
  "Nala Cat, adopted from a shelter, set a Guinness World Record in 2020 for the most Instagram followers of a cat.",
  "Venus the Two-Faced Cat has a face split down the middle, black on one side and ginger on the other.",
  "Venus the Two-Faced Cat has one blue eye and one green eye, and first went viral in 2012.",
  "Colonel Meow, a Himalayan-Persian cross, set a Guinness World Record in 2014 for the longest fur on a cat.",
  "Hamilton the Hipster Cat is famous for white markings that look like a curled moustache.",
  "The 2011 Nyan Cat animation was modelled on Marty, a Russian Blue belonging to its creator Chris Torres.",
  "Marty, the real cat behind Nyan Cat, died in 2012.",
  "Henri, le Chat Noir, a tuxedo cat from Seattle, won the top prize at the first Internet Cat Video Festival in 2012.",
  "Sockington, a grey and white cat from Massachusetts, had more than a million followers on Twitter by 2010.",
  "Longcat, a long white cat from Japan whose real name was Nobiko, became an early internet meme in the 2000s.",
  "Smoothie, a British Longhair from the Netherlands, became an Instagram star in the mid 2010s.",
  "Pudge, a female Exotic Shorthair from Minneapolis, became internet famous for a white marking like a moustache.",
  "In 1996 a stray cat named Scarlett carried her five kittens one by one out of a burning garage in Brooklyn.",
  "Scarlett was badly burned saving her kittens, and thousands of people offered to adopt her and the kittens.",
  "The North Shore Animal League named its Scarlett Award for Animal Heroism after the Brooklyn fire cat.",
  "In 2014 a cat named Tara chased off a dog that was attacking a four-year-old boy in Bakersfield, California.",
  "Tara the hero cat was filmed by a home security camera, and the video was viewed tens of millions of times.",
  "Tara was the first cat to win the Los Angeles SPCA's Hero Dog Award, in 2015.",
  "Oscar, a cat from Jersey, received two prosthetic back feet in 2010 after losing them in a combine harvester accident.",
  "Oscar the bionic cat's implants were fitted by the surgeon Noel Fitzpatrick, later known from the TV show Supervet.",
  "Holly, a tortoiseshell cat, found her way about 300 kilometres home to West Palm Beach, Florida, in 2012.",
  "Holly the Florida cat was identified by her microchip when she turned up a mile from home two months later.",
  "Emily, a cat from Wisconsin, was shipped by accident to France in a cargo container in 2005 and flown home.",
  "Emily the stowaway cat was flown back from France to the United States in business class.",
  "Blackie, a cat in Britain, inherited around 7 million pounds in 1988 and is listed as the richest cat ever.",
  "Tommaso, a stray taken in by a Rome widow, reportedly inherited a fortune of about 10 million euros in 2011.",
  "Pudding, a shelter cat in Wisconsin, roused his new owner during a diabetic seizure on his very first night home.",
  "A cat named Masha was reported to have kept an abandoned baby warm in a stairwell in Obninsk, Russia, in 2015.",
  "Fred the Undercover Kitty helped Brooklyn prosecutors catch a man posing as a vet in 2006.",
  "Fred the Undercover Kitty received a Law Enforcement Appreciation Award from the Brooklyn District Attorney.",
  "Homer, a blind cat, was the subject of Gwen Cooper's 2009 bestseller Homer's Odyssey.",
  "Jack the Cat escaped his carrier at New York's JFK Airport in 2011 and was found in the terminal 61 days later.",
  "Sugar, a cat from Boston, survived a fall from a 19th-floor window in 2012 with only minor injuries.",
  "The Hermitage Museum in St Petersburg keeps dozens of cats in its cellars to guard the collections against mice.",
  "The Hermitage cats trace their job back to a decree by Empress Elizabeth of Russia in 1745.",
  "Achilles, a deaf white cat from the Hermitage, was used to predict match results at the 2018 World Cup in Russia.",
  "The Hermitage Museum holds an annual Day of the Hermitage Cat to celebrate its feline staff.",
  "Ta-Miu, the cat of the Egyptian crown prince Thutmose, was buried in a carved limestone sarcophagus around 1350 BC.",
  "Ta-Miu's sarcophagus shows the cat seated before an offering table and is kept in the Egyptian Museum in Cairo.",
  "Nedjem, meaning sweet or pleasant, is the earliest known name given to a pet cat, recorded in Egypt around 1450 BC.",
  "Pangur Ban, a white cat, is the subject of a poem written by an Irish monk in the 9th century.",
  "The poem about Pangur Ban survives in a 9th-century manuscript kept at the abbey of St Paul in Carinthia, Austria.",
  "Selima, Horace Walpole's cat, drowned in a bowl of goldfish and was mourned in a 1747 poem by Thomas Gray.",
  "Sir Walter Scott's cat Hinse ruled his dogs for years but was killed by his bloodhound Nimrod in 1826.",
  "Charles Dickens's cat Williamina, originally named William, insisted on raising her kittens in his study.",
  "Micetto, the cat of Pope Leo XII, was born in the Vatican and later lived with the French writer Chateaubriand.",
  "Trixie, the Earl of Southampton's cat, is said to have found him in the Tower of London and is in his 1603 portrait.",
  "Theodore Roosevelt had a kitten named Tom Quartz after a cat in a Mark Twain story.",
  "A cat named Mourka was reported by The Times in 1943 to have carried messages for Soviet troops in Stalingrad.",
  "Nora the Piano Cat, a tabby from Philadelphia, inspired a 2009 orchestral work called CATcerto by a Lithuanian composer.",
  "Jorts, an orange office cat, became an internet star in 2021 after a Reddit post about his workplace antics.",
  "Beerbohm, a tabby who lived for about 20 years at a West End theatre in London, got an obituary in The Stage in 1995.",
  "Shironeko, a white cat from Japan known online as Basket Cat, was famous for dozing with fruit balanced on his head.",
  "Snowball, the cat whose hairs helped convict a killer in Canada, belonged to the suspect's parents.",
  "Faith the church cat's kitten, born in 1940, was a black and white cat named Panda.",
  "Posters of Baker and Taylor the library cats hung in libraries across the United States.",
  "Mittens the Wellington cat was nominated for New Zealander of the Year in 2020.",
  "Hank the Cat's campaign claimed he received thousands of write-in votes in Virginia's 2012 Senate race.",
  "Mark Twain's notice for the lost cat Bambino described him as large and intensely black, with thick velvety fur.",
  "Smudge, the cat at Glasgow's People's Palace museum, was made a member of a trade union in the 1980s.",
  "A Siamese cat called Chester was listed as co-author F. D. C. Willard on a 1975 physics paper by Jack Hetherington.",
  "Jack Hetherington listed his cat Chester as co-author because his paper said we and he was the only human author.",
  "Orangey the cat also starred in the 1951 film Rhubarb as a cat who inherits a baseball team.",
  "The hairless cat in the Austin Powers films was played by a Sphynx named Ted Nude-Gent.",
  "Morris, the 9Lives cat food mascot, ran a publicity campaign for US president in 1988.",
}

-- The wild cousins (234)
add {
  "Lions are the only truly social cats, living in family groups called prides.",
  "A lion pride is built around related females. The lionesses usually stay for life while males come and go.",
  "A lion's roar can be heard up to 8 km (5 miles) away.",
  "A male lion's mane grows darker and fuller as he matures, and lionesses tend to prefer males with darker manes.",
  "Lionesses do most of the hunting for a pride, often working together to surround prey.",
  "Wild lions survive today in sub-Saharan Africa and in one small population in India's Gir Forest.",
  "Asiatic lions have a fold of skin along the belly that African lions usually lack, and males have thinner manes.",
  "Lions spend most of the day resting and may sleep or doze for up to 20 hours.",
  "White lions are not albinos. Their pale coat comes from a recessive gene found in South Africa's Timbavati area.",
  "Lion cubs are born with faint spots on their coat, and the spots usually fade as they grow up.",
  "The lion is the only cat with a tuft of dark hair at the tip of its tail.",
  "Lions are the only cats in which males and females look clearly different, thanks to the male's mane.",
  "A snow leopard's tail is nearly as long as its body and helps it balance on steep, rocky slopes.",
  "Snow leopards wrap their thick tails around their bodies like a scarf to keep warm when resting.",
  "Snow leopards live in the mountains of Central and South Asia, often above 3,000 metres (about 10,000 feet).",
  "Unlike lions and tigers, a snow leopard cannot roar. It makes a puffing sound called a chuff instead.",
  "Snow leopards are so hard to spot in the wild that they are nicknamed the Ghost of the Mountains.",
  "A snow leopard's wide, furry paws act like snowshoes, spreading its weight on deep snow.",
  "Snow leopards have large nasal cavities that warm the thin, cold mountain air before it reaches the lungs.",
  "Snow leopards are powerful jumpers, reported to clear gaps of up to 15 metres (50 feet).",
  "The main prey of snow leopards are wild mountain sheep and goats such as blue sheep and ibex.",
  "Snow leopards have pale green or grey eyes, while most other big cats have yellow or amber eyes.",
  "Snow leopards live in 12 countries, including China, Mongolia, India, Nepal, Bhutan and Pakistan.",
  "In 2017 the IUCN, the global conservation body, moved the snow leopard from Endangered to Vulnerable.",
  "Relative to its skull size, the clouded leopard has the longest canine teeth of any living cat.",
  "Clouded leopards can climb down tree trunks head-first, something very few cats can do.",
  "A clouded leopard can hang upside down from a branch by its hind feet, thanks to flexible ankle joints.",
  "The clouded leopard is named for the large cloud-shaped blotches on its coat.",
  "Despite its name, the clouded leopard is not a type of leopard. It belongs to its own genus, Neofelis.",
  "The Sunda clouded leopard of Borneo and Sumatra was recognised as a separate species in 2006.",
  "Clouded leopards have short legs, big paws and a very long tail, all suited to life in the trees.",
  "Clouded leopards are found from the Himalayan foothills through Southeast Asia to southern China.",
  "Clouded leopards are so secretive that much of what is known about them comes from animals in zoos.",
  "Clouded leopards are listed as Vulnerable, threatened by forest loss and hunting for their skins.",
  "The sand cat is the only cat that lives mainly in true deserts, from the Sahara to Central Asia.",
  "Thick fur on the soles of a sand cat's feet protects it from scorching sand and hides its footprints.",
  "Sand cats can go for weeks without drinking, getting the water they need from their prey.",
  "Sand cats hunt at night and spend the hot desert day in burrows, often ones dug by other animals.",
  "Sand cats are skilled snake hunters and will even take on venomous vipers.",
  "A sand cat has large, low-set ears that pick up the faint sounds of prey moving under the sand.",
  "A sand cat's pale sandy coat blends in so well that the cat almost vanishes when it crouches on the sand.",
  "Sand cats are about the size of a small house cat but have a broader head and shorter legs.",
  "Sand cats cope with desert extremes, from freezing nights to ground temperatures above 50 C (122 F).",
  "The sand cat's scientific name, Felis margarita, honours a French officer whose expedition found it in 1858.",
  "Pallas's cat, also called the manul, has round pupils, unlike the vertical slit pupils of most small cats.",
  "Pallas's cat has the longest and densest fur of any wild cat, which keeps it warm on the cold Asian steppes.",
  "The manul's thick fur makes it look much bigger than it is. Underneath, it weighs about as much as a house cat.",
  "Pallas's cat is named after Peter Simon Pallas, a German naturalist who described it in 1776.",
  "Pallas's cats have flat faces and low-set ears, which help them peer over rocks without being seen.",
  "The manul's flat face and round pupils give it an unusually expressive, often grumpy-looking appearance.",
  "Pallas's cats live across the steppes and mountains of Central Asia, from Iran to Mongolia and western China.",
  "Pallas's cats mainly hunt pikas, small rabbit relatives, and often ambush them at their burrow entrances.",
  "Pallas's cats are poor runners and rely on hiding and ambush rather than speed to catch prey.",
  "Droppings collected on Mount Everest showed that Pallas's cats live there at over 5,000 metres (16,400 feet).",
  "Fishing cats live in the wetlands of South and Southeast Asia and are strong, willing swimmers.",
  "A fishing cat will dive head-first into water to catch fish and can swim underwater.",
  "Fishing cats have been seen tapping the water's surface with a paw, apparently to lure fish within reach.",
  "A fishing cat has a double-layered coat. A dense inner layer keeps its skin dry while it swims.",
  "The fishing cat is about twice the size of a house cat, with a stocky body and a short tail.",
  "A fishing cat's claws do not retract fully, so their tips show even when the cat is relaxed.",
  "The fishing cat is the state animal of West Bengal in India.",
  "Fishing cats are listed as Vulnerable, mainly because their wetland homes are being drained and built over.",
  "Fishing cats eat more than fish. They also take frogs, crabs, snakes, birds and small mammals.",
  "Fishing cats live in the mangrove forests of the Sundarbans, shared by India and Bangladesh.",
  "Fishing cats also live in Sri Lanka, where they have been recorded in the suburbs of Colombo.",
  "The black-footed cat of southern Africa is the smallest wild cat in Africa, weighing just 1 to 2.5 kg.",
  "The black-footed cat is often called the deadliest cat on Earth: about 60 percent of its hunts end in a kill.",
  "A black-footed cat may catch 10 to 14 small animals in a single night, far more than most cats.",
  "Black-footed cats spend the day in abandoned termite mounds or burrows, earning the nickname anthill tiger.",
  "Only the soles of a black-footed cat's feet are black. The rest of its coat is tawny with dark spots.",
  "Black-footed cats are found only in the dry grasslands and scrub of South Africa, Namibia and Botswana.",
  "A black-footed cat may walk 8 km (5 miles) or more in a single night of hunting.",
  "Despite its tiny size, a black-footed cat has been known to kill Cape hares heavier than itself.",
  "Black-footed cats are listed as Vulnerable, with fewer than 10,000 adults thought to remain in the wild.",
  "Black-footed cats are strictly nocturnal and almost never seen by day, which makes them hard to study.",
  "The rusty-spotted cat of India and Sri Lanka is the smallest wild cat, weighing about 1 to 1.6 kg as an adult.",
  "A full-grown rusty-spotted cat is only about half the size of a typical house cat.",
  "The rusty-spotted cat is named for the rust-coloured spots that run along its grey-brown back and sides.",
  "Rusty-spotted cats were long thought to live only in India and Sri Lanka, but they have also been found in Nepal.",
  "Rusty-spotted cats are nimble climbers and hunt mainly at night for rodents, birds, lizards and insects.",
  "Rusty-spotted cats are sometimes called the hummingbird of the cat family because they are so small and quick.",
  "The flat-headed cat of Southeast Asia has a long, flattened skull and small ears set low on its head.",
  "Flat-headed cats live along rivers and swamps in Borneo, Sumatra and the Malay Peninsula, feeding mainly on fish.",
  "A flat-headed cat's eyes face forward and sit close together, giving it sharp depth perception for catching fish.",
  "The flat-headed cat's teeth are unusually sharp and pointed for a cat, well suited to gripping slippery prey.",
  "The flat-headed cat is listed as Endangered, mainly because the lowland wetlands it depends on are being cleared.",
  "The flat-headed cat is one of the least known cats in the world, and most recent records come from camera traps.",
  "The margay can rotate its ankles up to 180 degrees, letting it run head-first down a tree trunk like a squirrel.",
  "A margay can hang from a branch by one hind foot, leaving its front paws free to grab prey.",
  "Margays spend most of their lives in the trees of Central and South American rainforests.",
  "A margay looks like a small ocelot but has a longer tail and a lighter build suited to climbing.",
  "In Brazil, a margay was seen mimicking the calls of baby pied tamarin monkeys, apparently to lure the adults.",
  "Margays have very large eyes for their size, which help them hunt birds, tree frogs and small mammals at night.",
  "Margays usually give birth to a single kitten, one reason their numbers recover slowly from losses.",
  "With its long body, short legs and small flat head, the jaguarundi looks more like an otter than a typical cat.",
  "Jaguarundis come in two main colours, dark grey and reddish brown, and both can appear in the same litter.",
  "Unlike most small cats, the jaguarundi is active mainly by day and often hunts in the morning.",
  "The jaguarundi's closest living relative is the puma, even though it is not much bigger than a house cat.",
  "Jaguarundis are unusually vocal for a cat, with at least 13 distinct calls recorded.",
  "The jaguarundi's coat is plain, with no spots or stripes, which is rare among the small cats of the Americas.",
  "The kodkod, or guina, of Chile and Argentina is the smallest cat in the Americas, weighing about 2 kg.",
  "Kodkods live mainly in the temperate rainforests of southern Chile and are expert climbers.",
  "Black kodkods are fairly common, and their spots can still be seen faintly in the right light.",
  "Kodkods feed mainly on rodents, birds and lizards, and sometimes raid farm chicken coops.",
  "Kodkods are listed as Vulnerable, mainly because the Chilean forests they depend on are being logged.",
  "The oncilla, also called the little spotted cat, is about the size of a house cat but more slender.",
  "Oncillas live in forests from Costa Rica to northern Argentina, often in cool cloud forests high in the mountains.",
  "In 2013 genetic studies showed that Brazil's oncillas are really two separate species that do not interbreed.",
  "Oncillas are hard to tell from margays and ocelots, but they are smaller and have a narrower face.",
  "Geoffroy's cats have been seen standing on their hind legs to scan their surroundings, using the tail for support.",
  "Geoffroy's cats range from Bolivia and southern Brazil down to Patagonia, further south than almost any other cat.",
  "Black Geoffroy's cats are common in some areas, and the species was once heavily hunted for its spotted fur.",
  "The Andean mountain cat lives high in the Andes, usually above 3,000 metres, among rocks and sparse grass.",
  "The Andean mountain cat is one of the rarest cats in the world, with fewer than 1,500 adults thought to survive.",
  "The Andean mountain cat has a long, bushy tail with dark rings that helps it balance on rocky slopes.",
  "The Andean mountain cat's main prey is the mountain viscacha, a rabbit-like rodent of the high Andes.",
  "The pampas cat's coat varies so much across South America that some scientists split it into several species.",
  "Despite its name, the pampas cat lives not only on grasslands but also in dry forests and high in the Andes.",
  "Pampas cats have a ridge of longer fur running along the spine that can look like a short mane.",
  "The bay cat is found only on the island of Borneo and is one of the least known cats on Earth.",
  "The bay cat is so rare that scientists did not examine a live one until 1992, over a century after it was named.",
  "Bay cats come in two colours, a rich chestnut red and a rarer grey, and have a long tail with a pale underside.",
  "The bay cat is listed as Endangered as Borneo's forests are cleared for logging and oil palm plantations.",
  "The Asian golden cat comes in many coat colours, from reddish gold to grey, black and even a spotted form.",
  "The Asian golden cat's closest relative is the bay cat of Borneo, which looks like a smaller version of it.",
  "Asian golden cats range from Nepal and northeast India through Southeast Asia to southern China and Sumatra.",
  "The African golden cat lives only in the rainforests of West and Central Africa and is rarely seen.",
  "Despite its name, the African golden cat may be reddish-brown, grey or occasionally black.",
  "The African golden cat is closely related to the caracal and serval, not to the Asian golden cat.",
  "The marbled cat of Southeast Asia looks like a miniature clouded leopard, with blotched fur and a very long tail.",
  "A marbled cat's thick, bushy tail is about as long as its head and body combined.",
  "Marbled cats are among the most tree-loving of all cats and hunt squirrels and birds high in the canopy.",
  "The marbled cat is about the size of a house cat, and its closest relatives are the bay cat and Asian golden cat.",
  "The leopard cat is the most widespread wild cat in Asia, found from Pakistan to Siberia and Indonesia.",
  "The leopard cat is the wild parent species of the Bengal breed, but in the wild it is a shy forest hunter.",
  "Leopard cats are about the size of a house cat, with longer legs and two white stripes running up from the eyes.",
  "Leopard cats in the cold north, such as the Amur region, are bigger and paler than those in the tropics.",
  "The Iriomote cat lives only on Iriomote, a small Japanese island, and is now treated as a type of leopard cat.",
  "The Iriomote cat was unknown to science until 1965, and only about 100 of them are thought to exist.",
  "Iriomote cats live on an island of under 300 square km, one of the smallest ranges of any wild cat.",
  "Despite its name, the jungle cat prefers reed beds, marshes and riverbanks to dense forest.",
  "The jungle cat, also called the reed cat, ranges from Egypt through the Middle East to Southeast Asia.",
  "The jungle cat is the largest living member of Felis, the group of small cats that also includes the wildcat.",
  "The Chinese mountain cat is found only in China, on the eastern edge of the Tibetan Plateau.",
  "The Chinese mountain cat was first photographed in the wild in 2007, by camera traps in Sichuan.",
  "The Chinese mountain cat has a sandy coat, faint stripes, a bushy ringed tail and small tufts on its ear tips.",
  "The European wildcat looks like a large, heavily built tabby with a thick, blunt-tipped tail ringed in black.",
  "European wildcats live in forests from Portugal and Scotland east to the Caucasus, and also on Sicily.",
  "The Scottish wildcat is Britain's only native wild cat, and interbreeding with domestic cats is its biggest threat.",
  "Scottish wildcats have mixed so much with domestic cats that in 2019 experts judged the wild population not viable.",
  "Captive-bred wildcats have been released in Scotland's Cairngorms since 2023 to rebuild the wild population.",
  "The African wildcat is the wild ancestor of the domestic cat, and the two can still interbreed freely.",
  "African wildcats have longer legs than house cats, giving them a taller, more upright look when sitting.",
  "The African wildcat has reddish fur on the backs of its ears, a quick way to tell it from a tabby.",
  "In 2002 fewer than 100 Iberian lynx survived, making it the most endangered cat in the world at the time.",
  "Thanks to captive breeding and releases, the Iberian lynx population passed 2,000 animals by 2024.",
  "In 2024 the Iberian lynx was moved from Endangered to Vulnerable, a rare conservation success for a cat.",
  "The Iberian lynx depends heavily on rabbits, which make up the great majority of its diet.",
  "Diseases that wiped out wild rabbits in Spain were a major cause of the Iberian lynx's decline.",
  "Iberian lynx are smaller than Eurasian lynx, with a more spotted coat and a beard of long fur on the cheeks.",
  "The Canada lynx has huge furry paws that work like snowshoes, letting it chase hares across deep snow.",
  "Canada lynx numbers rise and fall in a roughly 10-year cycle that follows the boom and bust of snowshoe hares.",
  "A Canada lynx's hind legs are longer than its front legs, giving it a slightly stooped, forward-tilting stance.",
  "Canada lynx were released in Colorado from 1999 to 2006 to return the species to the southern Rockies.",
  "The Eurasian lynx is the largest of the four lynx species and can weigh more than 25 kg (55 pounds).",
  "Unlike the smaller lynxes, the Eurasian lynx often hunts deer, taking roe deer and even young red deer.",
  "Eurasian lynx range from Scandinavia and the Alps across Russia to the Himalayas and the Pacific coast of Siberia.",
  "Hunted out of much of Western Europe, the Eurasian lynx has been reintroduced to places such as the Swiss Alps.",
  "A bobcat's tail is black only on top with a white underside, while a lynx's tail tip is black all round.",
  "Bobcats are the most common wild cat in North America, with a population thought to number in the millions.",
  "Bobcats thrive in a huge range of habitats, from swamps and deserts to forests and the edges of suburbs.",
  "A bobcat can kill prey as large as an adult deer, though rabbits and rodents are its usual meals.",
  "Every ocelot has its own coat pattern, and the markings on its left and right sides do not match.",
  "Ocelot fur was so fashionable in the 1960s and 1970s that the species was hunted hard until the trade was banned.",
  "Fewer than 100 ocelots remain in the United States, nearly all in the dense brush country of southern Texas.",
  "Ocelots are the largest of the small spotted cats of the Americas, weighing up to about 15 kg (33 pounds).",
  "Servals succeed in about half of their hunting attempts, a far higher rate than most cats.",
  "A serval can hear rodents moving underground and will dig them out with its long front legs.",
  "Servals often hunt near water, wading into marshes for frogs and fish as well as rodents.",
  "All-black servals are occasionally seen, especially in the highlands of Kenya.",
  "The caracal's name comes from a Turkish word meaning black ear.",
  "Caracals can live in near-waterless deserts, getting most of the moisture they need from their prey.",
  "In southern Africa caracals are often killed by farmers for taking sheep and goats, a major threat to them there.",
  "Caracals hunt mainly at night and are seldom seen, even in areas where they are fairly common.",
  "The puma is the largest of the purring cats, and in the Americas only the jaguar is bigger.",
  "Pumas can jump about 5.5 metres (18 feet) straight up from a standstill.",
  "Puma kittens are born with spotted coats and blue eyes, and both fade as they grow up.",
  "The Florida panther is a puma whose numbers fell to a few dozen in the 1970s. Today an estimated 120 to 230 remain.",
  "In 1995 eight female pumas from Texas were released in Florida to add fresh genes to the inbred panthers.",
  "In proportion to its body, the puma has the longest hind legs of any cat, which power its enormous leaps.",
  "The Amur leopard of the Russian Far East is among the rarest big cats, with only around 100 left in the wild.",
  "Amur leopards grow a pale winter coat with hair up to 7 cm (nearly 3 inches) long to cope with deep snow.",
  "The Arabian leopard is the smallest leopard subspecies and is critically endangered, with fewer than 200 left.",
  "Wild Arabian leopards survive mainly in the mountains of Oman and Yemen.",
  "Black leopards are most common in Southeast Asia, and on the Malay Peninsula almost all leopards are black.",
  "Unlike other big cats, which usually bite the throat, a jaguar often kills with a single bite through the skull.",
  "Jaguars eat caimans and river turtles, and their jaws are strong enough to crack a turtle's shell.",
  "A jaguar's rosettes often have small dark spots inside them, while a leopard's are usually empty.",
  "Jaguars once ranged into the southern United States, and lone males still wander north from Mexico into Arizona.",
  "Jaguars from Brazil's Pantanal wetlands are the largest of all, far heavier than those of Central America.",
  "Many scientists now group tigers into just two subspecies, the mainland tiger and the Sunda Island tiger.",
  "Three tiger subspecies, the Bali, Javan and Caspian tigers, died out during the 20th century.",
  "The Sumatran tiger is the smallest living tiger, and only a few hundred survive on the island of Sumatra.",
  "Amur tigers of the Russian Far East endure winters below minus 30 C, helped by thick fur and a layer of fat.",
  "India is home to roughly 70 percent of the world's wild tigers.",
  "Wild tiger numbers fell to about 3,200 in 2010, but have since risen to more than 4,500.",
  "The king cheetah's bold blotches and stripes come from one recessive gene. It was once thought a separate species.",
  "Cheetahs were brought back to India in 2022, some 70 years after the country's last wild cheetahs were killed.",
  "Cheetahs chirp like birds, purr and make a courtship call known as a stutter-bark.",
  "Cheetahs have very low genetic diversity, thought to stem from a population crash around 10,000 years ago.",
  "There are about 40 species of wild cat alive today, native to every continent except Australia and Antarctica.",
  "Only five living cats belong to Panthera, the big cat genus: the lion, tiger, leopard, jaguar and snow leopard.",
  "Roaring cats such as lions and tigers cannot purr the way small cats do, and small cats cannot roar.",
  "A roaring cat's hyoid, a bone in the throat, is only partly hardened. In purring cats it is fully bony and rigid.",
  "Despite their size, the cheetah and the puma are grouped with the small cats rather than with the roaring big cats.",
  "Smilodon, the famous sabre-toothed cat, was not an ancestor of today's cats but a cousin on a branch that died out.",
  "Sabre-toothed cats such as Smilodon died out around 10,000 years ago, at the end of the last ice age.",
  "The oldest known cat, Proailurus, lived around 25 million years ago. Its fossils were first found in France.",
  "Cats reached the Americas by crossing from Asia over the Bering land bridge when sea levels were low.",
  "The cheetah's ancestors probably arose in North America and crossed back to Asia over the Bering land bridge.",
  "A liger, the offspring of a male lion and a female tiger, is bred only in captivity and often outgrows both parents.",
  "A tigon has a tiger father and a lion mother. Tigons are rarer than ligers and usually no bigger than their parents.",
  "Lions and tigers no longer share any wild range, so ligers and tigons are known only from captivity.",
  "Most wild cats hunt by ambush, stalking close, rushing the last few metres and killing with a bite to the neck.",
  "Most wild cats spend well over half of each day asleep or resting, saving energy for short bursts of hunting.",
  "India is home to 15 species of wild cat, more than any other country.",
  "The largest wild cats, tigers, can weigh more than 100 times as much as the tiny rusty-spotted cat.",
  "Habitat loss, poaching and conflict with farmers are the main threats facing wild cats around the world.",
  "A black panther is not a species of its own. It is a leopard or a jaguar whose genes make its coat dark.",
  "The gene that makes a jaguar black is dominant, while the one that makes a leopard black is recessive.",
  "White tigers are not albinos. A recessive gene gives them a white coat and blue eyes, but they keep their stripes.",
  "Nearly all white tigers alive today descend from one wild male caught in central India in 1951.",
  "White tigers are almost unknown in the wild, and the last known wild one was shot in 1958.",
  "The tiger is the largest cat alive, and big wild males can weigh more than 200 kg (440 pounds).",
}

-- Cats in words, stories, screens and folklore (252)
add {
  "The English word cat comes from the Late Latin cattus, which replaced the older Latin word for a cat, feles.",
  "The word feline comes from feles, the Latin word the Romans used for cats before cattus took over.",
  "Irish cat, Welsh cath, German Katze, Polish kot and Basque katu all share the Latin root cattus.",
  "In French a cat is a chat, in Spanish and Portuguese a gato, in Italian a gatto and in Dutch a kat.",
  "In Russian a male cat is a kot and a female cat is a koshka.",
  "The Japanese word for cat is neko, and Japanese cats are said to go nyan rather than meow.",
  "In Mandarin Chinese the word for cat is mao, which sounds much like the noise a cat makes.",
  "The Arabic word for a cat is qitt for a male and qitta for a female.",
  "In Hindi and Urdu a cat is a billi, in Finnish a kissa, in Turkish a kedi and in Tagalog a pusa.",
  "Kitten came into English in the Middle Ages from an Old French word that was a diminutive of chat.",
  "Puss, a word for calling a cat, has been used in English since the 1500s and gave Puss in Boots his name.",
  "Moggy is a British word for an ordinary house cat of no particular breed.",
  "Tabby comes from Attabiyah, a district of Baghdad known for striped silk. The cat was named after the cloth.",
  "Catgut, used for violin strings and surgical stitches, was made from the guts of sheep and goats, never cats.",
  "The cat o' nine tails was a whip of nine knotted cords used for punishment in the British navy and army.",
  "A catwalk was a narrow walkway on a ship, bridge or stage long before the word was used for fashion runways.",
  "A catnap is a short, light sleep, named for the way cats doze during the day.",
  "The word copycat, for someone who imitates others, is recorded in American English from the late 1800s.",
  "A cat burglar is a thief who climbs in through upper windows or roofs, a term that dates from the early 1900s.",
  "The cat's pajamas, the cat's whiskers and the cat's meow were all 1920s American slang for something excellent.",
  "In jazz slang of the 1930s a cat was a musician or a fan, and a cool cat was someone admirably relaxed.",
  "Cab Calloway's Hepster's Dictionary of 1938 defined a cat as a swing musician or a lover of swing music.",
  "The saying raining cats and dogs was in print by the 1700s, and nobody knows for certain where it came from.",
  "The question about a cat having got someone's tongue is recorded from the mid-1800s, and its origin is unknown.",
  "To let the cat out of the bag, meaning to give away a secret, appears in print from the 1760s.",
  "Curiosity killed the cat dates from the late 1800s. The older form, from the 1590s, was care killed the cat.",
  "In the old saying care killed the cat, used by Shakespeare and Ben Jonson, care meant worry.",
  "A cat may look at a king, meaning even the lowly have some rights, appears in an English proverb collection of 1546.",
  "The proverb when the cat's away the mice will play has been used in English since at least the early 1600s.",
  "No room to swing a cat has described a cramped space since the 1660s. Its link to the cat o' nine tails is unproven.",
  "Like herding cats, for a hopeless attempt to organize people, was popularized by a US television advert in 2000.",
  "The phrase grin like a Cheshire cat was recorded in the 1780s, long before Lewis Carroll's Alice met the cat.",
  "A fat cat, meaning a wealthy backer or a well-paid boss, is American slang recorded from the 1920s.",
  "In the catbird seat, meaning in a strong position, was popularized by the baseball broadcaster Red Barber.",
  "Catty-corner comes from cater-corner, with cater from the French word for four. It has nothing to do with cats.",
  "Caterpillar probably comes from an Old French word meaning hairy cat, chatepelose.",
  "Catkins, the fluffy flower spikes of willows and hazels, take their name from a Dutch word meaning little cat.",
  "Catfish are named for the whisker-like feelers around their mouths, which look like a cat's whiskers.",
  "The catcall was originally a squeaky whistle used by 1600s theatre audiences to jeer at bad plays.",
  "A group of cats is sometimes called a clowder, a word that is a variant of clutter.",
  "An old word for a litter of kittens is a kindle, from a verb meaning to give birth.",
  "The word tomcat caught on after a 1760 book, The Life and Adventures of a Cat, made its hero Tom famous.",
  "The French saying appeler un chat un chat, to call a cat a cat, means to speak plainly, like calling a spade a spade.",
  "In German a Katzenjammer, literally the wailing of cats, is a hangover. The word is also used in English.",
  "The Katzenjammer Kids, a comic strip begun in 1897 and one of the oldest in the world, contains no cats at all.",
  "The Japanese saying neko no te mo karitai, wanting to borrow even a cat's paws, means being desperate for help.",
  "Cat's cradle, the string game played between two people's hands, has a name whose origin nobody has explained.",
  "Online, paying the cat tax means posting a photo of a cat after mentioning it in a post.",
  "In English cats have nine lives. In Spanish, Italian and German sayings they have seven.",
  "Shakespeare's Mercutio calls Tybalt the king of cats in Romeo and Juliet and taunts him about his nine lives.",
  "Shakespeare's witches in Macbeth take their cue from a cat: thrice the brinded cat hath mewed.",
  "The word for a cat lover is ailurophile, from the Greek ailouros, meaning cat. A cat hater is an ailurophobe.",
  "Abu Hurairah, a companion of the prophet Muhammad, bears a name meaning father of the kitten.",
  "Pangur Ban is a 9th century Old Irish poem about a monk and his cat. Ban means white.",
  "In Pangur Ban the monk hunts words as his cat hunts mice. The manuscript is kept in an abbey in Austria.",
  "Charles Perrault published Puss in Boots in 1697 under the title The Master Cat, or the Cat in Boots.",
  "The Puss in Boots story is older than Perrault. An Italian version by Straparola appeared in the 1550s.",
  "The Brothers Grimm dropped Puss in Boots from their collection after the first edition because it was too French.",
  "Dick Whittington's cat is folklore. The real Richard Whittington was Lord Mayor of London, but no cat is recorded.",
  "The Cheshire Cat in Alice's Adventures in Wonderland (1865) can vanish slowly, leaving only its grin behind.",
  "T. S. Eliot's Old Possum's Book of Practical Cats (1939) began as poems written in letters to his godchildren.",
  "Eliot's cats include Skimbleshanks the Railway Cat, Mr Mistoffelees the conjurer and Macavity the mystery cat.",
  "Macavity is called the Napoleon of Crime, a title Eliot borrowed from Sherlock Holmes's description of Moriarty.",
  "The musical Cats by Andrew Lloyd Webber opened in London in 1981 and on Broadway in 1982.",
  "Cats ran for 21 years in London and was the longest-running West End musical until Les Miserables passed it in 2006.",
  "Grizabella, who sings Memory in Cats, is not in Eliot's book. She came from unpublished lines his widow supplied.",
  "Eliot's Jellicle cats are a playful squashing of dear little cats, and his Pollicle dogs are poor little dogs.",
